# Orchestrate, as the owner settled it on 9 Nov 2026: Plan, Dispatch and oversee, Summarise. A Job that
# takes a pile of work, splits it into Jobs, runs them and reports what they landed. It writes no code of
# its own. Each step is a plan group and `gate` names the fact Fleet sees for itself that ends it.
# `bug.json` beside this file says where the schema lives, and
# `.claude/decisions/2026-11-09-workflows-are-gated-plan-groups.md` has his answers.
#
# **Assess is folded into Plan**, and Dispatch into Oversee: neither ended on a fact Fleet sees.
#
# **`oversee` ends on `jobs_ended`**: every Job this one started has merged or been ended, ones started
# late included. Summarise was entered twice while those Jobs were still live when the rail guessed it.
# With some still open (dry run, 9 Nov), it points him in its own thread at a child waiting on him and
# waits; the child's need shows on its own row, not as a second item.
#
# **`summarise` lands a report**: a page he approves or sends back with notes, and no pull request.
{
  "version": 1,
  "workflow_id": "orchestrate",
  "name": "orchestrate",
  "for_requests": "A pile of work to split up and hand out: a batch of feedback, a list of issues or a milestone, where what is wanted is several Jobs run to land it and a report of what each landed. One change, however large, that one Job can land is a feature; working out how to build something before anybody builds it is a design plan.",
  "lands": "report",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "plan",
      "label": "Plan",
      "about": "Reads the pile of work, checks each item against main, and proposes one Job per piece as a plan. Ends when you approve the plan; no Job starts before then.",
      "instructions": "Read the work you were handed and every link in it. Check each item against main: done, partial or missing, with a path. Leave out what main already does, and say so.\nGroup what is left into pieces one Job can land as one pull request. Put pieces that touch the same files in one group, or order them.\nRecord the orchestration plan with record_plan: these workflow groups first, then under Dispatch and oversee one task per Job, each with the subagent type, paths, and what it gives. Say which run together and which wait.\nWait for the person to approve the plan. Start no Job before then. Edit nothing.",
      "gate": "plan_approved",
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "human_always"
    },
    {
      "id": "oversee",
      "label": "Dispatch and oversee",
      "about": "Starts a Job for each piece, two at a time, and follows them, stepping in when one is stuck. Ends when every Job it started has merged or been ended.",
      "instructions": "Start a Job for each piece with start_another_job. At most two run at once: start each of the rest with `after` on an earlier one, `pr_lands` where it builds on that Job's work, `ends` otherwise.\nFleet tells you when a Job you started ends or merges. End your turn between notices; never poll.\nWhen a Job is stuck, failing, or has asked you something, read its thread and message it. End it and start another only when it cannot recover. Start another Job whenever the work shows one is needed, and tell the person why in a line.\nWhen only Jobs waiting on the person are left, say in your thread which ones and what each waits on, once, then wait. Do not repeat their questions as your own.\nEdit nothing and open no pull request yourself.",
      "gate": "jobs_ended",
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    },
    {
      "id": "summarise",
      "label": "Summarise",
      "about": "Writes a report of what each Job landed, with its pull request, and the follow-up work. Ends when you approve it. No pull request is opened.",
      "instructions": "Load the writing-a-document skill and write one HTML page to .armada/documents/<subject>.html.\nConclusion first. Then a table with one row per Job you started: what it landed, its pull request as a link, and whether it merged or was ended, and why.\nThen a Follow-up work section: one row for each thing a Job left, deferred or exposed, saying what it is and where.\nAsk the person, one item at a time, whether to file each follow-up item as an issue or dispatch it as a Job, then do what he picks.\nAnswer every note on the page by changing the page where the note points. Open no pull request.",
      "gate": "document_approved",
      "phase": "delivery",
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "human_always"
    }
  ]
}
